# Bitcoin Lifeboat - Singlesig Recovery Runbook

## 1. Safety warning

Never type your seed words into a website, an app, or a search box.

Bitcoin Lifeboat never asks for your seed phrase. Anyone who does is trying to steal from you.

This runbook holds no secrets. Keep your seed words on paper or metal only, never on a phone or computer.

## 2. Do not panic

If you are reading this during an emergency, slow down.

Recovering a Bitcoin wallet is a careful, step-by-step process. Most mistakes come from rushing.

Take a break before each major step. Nothing in this runbook needs to be done in a hurry.

## 3. Stop and call a trusted helper

If any step is unclear, stop and ask a person you trust before continuing.

Do not let anyone watch you type your seed words or photograph your backups.

A trusted helper can be a family member, a friend, or a Bitcoin-literate advisor. Record who to call in section 9.

## 4. Required materials checklist

- [ ] This runbook, printed on paper.

- [ ] Your written or stamped descriptor backup.

- [ ] Your hardware wallet, or your seed backup.

- [ ] A computer with the wallet software listed in section 10.

## 5. Wallet type summary

Wallet type: singlesig.

- Script type: wpkh

- Number of keys: 1

## 6. Descriptor backup reminder

Your descriptor is the map to your wallet. Without it, recovery is much harder and sometimes impossible.

Keep a written or stamped copy of the descriptor with each seed backup. It contains no secrets, but it reveals your balance history, so store it as privately as your seed.

Descriptor: [descriptor redacted, see private export]

