Confirm your signing device powers on and that you hold its seed backup.

- Signer A: fingerprint f0f0f0f0, path m/84h/1h/0h

Signer A location: ______________________

## 8. Passphrase reminder

No passphrase was recorded for this wallet.

If you believe a passphrase was set, do not continue without it. A passphrase changes which wallet the seed words reach.

## 9. Emergency contacts

Fill these in by hand. Do not store the contact details of strangers or so-called recovery services here.

Trusted helper name: ______________________

Trusted helper phone: ______________________

Person who inherits this wallet: ______________________

Attorney or executor: ______________________

## 10. Wallet software dependencies

Recovery may need specific wallet software. Record what this wallet depends on:

- Sparrow

- Bitcoin Core

If that software stops working, your descriptor and seed still allow recovery with other BIP380-compatible wallet software.

## 11. Verification steps

1. Load this descriptor into your wallet software in WATCH-ONLY mode (no seed entered).

2. Confirm the first receive address shown matches an address you already have on record.

3. On a test network (signet or testnet), rehearse signing and broadcasting a small transaction with your device.

4. Record today's date in section 13 once the drill succeeds.

Rehearse this drill at least once every twelve months.

## 12. Stop conditions

Stop immediately and seek help if any of these happen:

- A website, app, or person asks you to type your seed words.

- A derived address does not match the address you expected.

- Anyone pressures you to hurry, to share your screen, or to send a test payment.

- The wallet software shows a balance or history you do not recognise.

When in doubt, stop and call the trusted helper recorded in section 9.

## 13. Date of last successful drill

